<title>HONG KONG: China securities regulator chief to retire - paper.</title>
<headline>China securities regulator chief to retire - paper.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chairman of the China Securities Regulatory Commission (CSRC) will retire in the near future and be replaced by one of his deputies, a Hong Kong newspaper reported on Friday.</p>
<p>Zhou Daojiong would step down as head of China's top securities watchdog and be replaced by Li Jiange, a former secretary to China's economic tsar Zhu Rongji, the Hong Kong Economic Times quoted unnamed sources as saying.</p>
<p>The change was a normal personnel change as Zhou had reached retirement age, the sources said.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
